  message: "DONE in PR #2030 (merged; dev 3b6463d531). DEFECT (read in code, measured before the edit on mlflow base_mlflow.json): verify_claims.unseeded_ingress_handlers read behavior_map[\"entrypoints\"], which detect_entrypoints had floored at rank_score >= 0.10 and capped at compute_entrypoint_cap(node_count) with a 0.4 per-kind share; mlflow had 302 route-handler candidates after the detector's own dedups, 200 in the capped list; the disclosure named 254 production handlers of all ingress kinds where the full list holds 320 (66 unnamed, 21%; the pre-registration's '401 / 107' came from a census of route symbols, see CORPUS). SHIPPED: entrypoints.detect_entrypoint_candidates (every candidate, ranked, before floor and cap) + apply_rank_floor_and_cap (the two halves of detect_entrypoints; its contract unchanged for every other reader) + request_ingress_entries(candidates) ({symbol_id, kind, label} per REQUEST_INGRESS_KINDS candidate, rank order); the survey writer (cli.py) writes top-level `request_ingress` beside `entrypoints` (schema 0.21.0 unreleased, additive; scripts/generate-schema property with the kind enum = REQUEST_INGRESS_KINDS; schema.py template; spec section; stripped from compact/tiered views like usage_contexts); verify_claims.ingress_candidates(map) = request_ingress when the key is present else entrypoints (older map: partial, nothing invented), fed to unseeded_ingress_handlers at the verify-claims call site; include_non_production keeps deciding test-code handlers. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE: production-path tests packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_request_ingress_uncapped.py (6 cases: 60 handlers under cap 50 -> entrypoints <= 50 and request_ingress == 60; capped list == candidates floored+capped; a test-file handler is under the floor yet an entry the disclosure's scope decides; non-ingress kinds excluded; the fallback; and END TO END survey -> artifact -> verify-claims --input: the disclosure counts 60 on the new artifact and 50 on the same artifact with the key removed) + test_compact strips it; mutations: ingress_candidates always falling back -> 2 red (fallback unit + end-to-end); writer omits the key -> 1 red (end-to-end); kind filter off -> 1 red; compact keeps the key -> 1 red (test_compact); rank floor off -> 1 red; size cap off -> 2 red; each exactly the predicted set, files restored byte-identical. CORPUS (base = losij tree content = dev 8f64e2e155 code; branch surveys with own caches; diff_ab.py; PREREGISTER.md / RESULT.md): P5 HELD: entrypoints byte-identical on mlflow (500) and flask-restful (32). mlflow request_ingress 356 entries (302 http_route, 50 graphql_server, 4 middleware_handler), 102 absent from the capped list; the disclosure's production-scope count 254 -> 320 (+66, old set a subset of the new), all scopes 254 -> 356. flask-restful (control, under the cap): 23 entries = the 12 capped + 11 test-path handlers under the rank floor (listed by design; the default-scope disclosure unchanged at 12). TWO PRE-REGISTERED NUMBERS REFUTED (P1 401 http_route, P3 12): the loss was sized by a census of route SYMBOLS (69 concept handlers + 332 markers); the detector's route-LABEL dedup (one entry per 'HTTP METHOD path' string, repo-wide) collapses 99 of them before any cap: 47 a marker onto its own handler (correct), 52 distinct code sharing a label, 6 on production paths (four mlflow gateway handlers all labelled 'HTTP GET <binop>'); filed as WI-rorug-tudul-jakar-zagoj-podob-sijop-maduv-sosos. The '107 production handlers' figure in the pre-registration came from that wrong instrument; the gain the cap and floor hid is 66. P2 (verify-claims on mlflow through the CLI, claims_generic.yaml): through the CLI with --input on the branch map and on the base map, the one untrusted_input claim not already violated (untrusted-input-no-database, inconclusive) names 320 request handlers on the branch map and 254 on the base map (no key -> the fallback); violated claims carry no reason by design. The pre-registered '>= 307 http handlers' is REFUTED on the number by the same label-dedup diagnosis; the mechanism held end to end. NOT ASSERTED: that the disclosure's handler set is COMPLETE for a framework whose handler is no entrypoint at all (WI-jonin's class, Go ServeHTTP now covered, others not surveyed); the narrowing per seeded framework (WI-ritog); any change to `entrypoints` (byte-identical on both repos by P5)."  # 204b
